From: jaylfc <jaylfc25@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: prefix and channel the amps

The two tfa9873 amplifiers register "Speaker" and "PWUP" as component-level
DAPM widgets. With no sound-name-prefix on either node the second instance
overwrites the first ("ASoC: sink widget PWUP overwritten"), the DAPM graph
never completes, and no backend DAI enables for MultiMedia1 -- leaving the
card with HDMI/DisplayPort controls only and no speaker path at all.

Give each amp a distinct prefix so the widgets no longer collide, and set
sound-channel so the pair renders true stereo rather than both amps playing
the same content. Also correct the stale EAR/SPK comments: these are the top
and bottom speakers of a stereo pair, not an earpiece and a main speaker.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -1021,21 +1021,27 @@
 	clock-frequency = <100000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
-	tfa9873_l: codec@34 { /* EAR */
+	tfa9873_l: codec@34 { /* Top speaker: RIGHT in the fixed landscape mount */
 		compatible = "nxp,tfa9873",
 			     "nxp,tfa9872";
 		reg = <0x34>;
 		reset-gpio = <&tlmm 101 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
+		sound-channel = <1>;
+		sound-name-prefix = "Amplifier R";
+
 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
 	};
 
-	tfa9873_r: codec@35 { /* SPK */
+	tfa9873_r: codec@35 { /* Bottom speaker: LEFT in the fixed landscape mount */
 		compatible = "nxp,tfa9873",
 			     "nxp,tfa9872";
 		reg = <0x35>;
 		reset-gpio = <&tlmm 101 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
+		sound-channel = <0>;
+		sound-name-prefix = "Amplifier L";
+
 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
 	};
 };
